Missing: _Generic is not parsed

_Generic is not supported: it is neither a keyword (src/init.c) nor swallowed in
fallback_defines (src/startup.c), so it parses as an identifier and every
association is a syntax error. Recovery happens to keep some references but
loses the default: branch and the typedef used as an association type, and
_Generic itself is recorded as a symbol.

Only parsing is needed, not branch selection (the controlling expression's type
and type compatibility): a keyword and a generic-selection rule with
type-name : assignment-expression and default : assignment-expression
associations. Swallowing it with a define would avoid the errors but drop the
function references, which is usually what _Generic selects between.
